dies by the vehicles  research foundation  the current vaccines are still effective  against the p1 strain  this vaccination center can administer  thousands of doses per day  but even here the authorities are unable  to implement  physical distancing  when vaccination starts there are always  a lot of people  but then the crowding goes down when  older people come for vaccination  they bring one or two relatives and  that's what  causes the crowd with more than seven  percent of its  inhabitants vaccinated the state of  amazonas  where manaus is located has administered  the most  doses to date in brazil however it is  still  far from containing the virus without  social distancing  people will continue to die from the  virus  the city has made space for 22 000 new  graves in the cemetery  it's a horrific forecast of what the new  covet variants could bring to manaus in  the near future  and journalist sam cowie joins me now  from sao paulo for more  sam as the u.s and parts of europe start  to get things more under control  brazil appears to be going in the wrong  direction with these crushing case  numbers  how did things get so out of control in  brazil  good morning claire yeah it's a really  dire situation here what we've seen  in manaus is essentially now spreading  across the country  where i am here in sao paulo which is  brazil's wealthiest and most developed  state  there are no more icu beds right now  there are thousands of people  a thousand people in fact waiting in the  queue  some people have died in the queue at  least a dozen people that we know of  have died  in the queue you know sao paulo is a  huge state 44 million people but it  really sets the tone if the richest  and most developed state in the country  is at full capacity  um essentially there are three main  problems here right now  what as the as we heard from our  colleague in the previous report  the new variant which was detected in  manaus in january  is one of the uh main cases of this what  we're seeing across the country right  now  is that the number of new cases that are  being detected it's something  like five out of eight are connected to  the new variant  it hasn't been proven necessarily the  new variant in itself is more deadly but  it is  more contagious it's twice as contagious  as the original coronavirus  and in a country like brazil if there's  more con if there's  if it's more contagious there's going to  be more people that die especially as  the hospitals  fill up the second reason is that the  vaccine uptake has been very slow across  the country  less than five percent of people have  been vaccine you know 220 million people  here in brazil  long way to go before we reach the 70  percent uh  threshold which is considered safe and  then the main reason that if you speak  to all medical professionals  is the behavior of the federal  government especially the far-right  president jaya bolsonaro who from the  beginning  has set to downplay the virus you know  when he was in florida with donald trump  it was  he said it was an invention of the media  to take down the government then it went  to being a little flu that he wouldn't  have to worry about because he used to  be an athlete then it went to being i'll  just man up we've got to get on with  things  and the thing is this kind of rhetoric  you know in brazil which is a country  it's a middle-income country lots of  people in the informal economy  lots of people you know literally  working during lunch time to put dinner  on the table  when a president says uh it won't affect  me because i used to be an  athlete you know that resonates but for  better or worse that resonates with a  lot of people  and so the loggerheads the the the the  the disconnect between the federal  government that we've seen here  and the state government here like we've  seen in sao paulo with the state  governor calling on people to really try  and you know  social distance and going to lockdown  and the president saying no we've got to  keep the economy open we've got to keep  the economy running it's just a little  flu  you know that's really caused a lot of  confusion and is one of the  main reasons uh for the high death toll  according to all the experts i've spoken  to  sam cowie in sao paulo thank you very  much for that update  you
 

